TRUENOISE — SYSTEM DOCUMENTATION
=================================
Generated May 2026 · Updated September 2026
For: Marty Krizan, truenoise.org

This document describes every system, service, and file that makes up the
TrueNoise platform. It is written for someone who understands the project
but may not remember every technical detail six months from now.

September 2026 update: the website has grown from four pages to nine, and a
substantial BRGHT departure-noise analysis was added (the sensitivity page and
its linked documents). The backend infrastructure — Render, Supabase, GitHub
Pages, GoDaddy DNS, Formspree, UptimeRobot — is unchanged except for one item:
main.py was extended to add wind, temperature, and humidity columns to the
observations table. Backend account details and endpoints below reflect the
original setup; re-verify against the live services if ever in doubt.

